#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:5
#: 2a9906a7bb9343c895e7c630c2ce5271
msgid "QRTL Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:7
#: fef853185d994b2c9d51e93254ef8081
msgid "QRTL mode (QuadPlane Return To Launch mode) navigates QuadPlane from its current position to hover above the home position and then land. The behavior of QRTL mode can be controlled by several adjustable parameters. This page describes how to use and customize QRTL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:13
#: d7e4c44b1823423f9549dc05994953a7
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:15
#: eff0635372dc47b290b5ef08a383f39f
msgid "When QRTL mode is selected, the QuadPlane will return to the home location. By default, it will transition to fixed wing mode (if in a VTOL mode before entering, it will climb to :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` if below that altitude, before transitioning), executing the first part of a normal RTL, and then make an approach  as it nears the landing point and switch to VTOL mode and proceed to the landing point, then descend to a landing. See the description of this under the :ref:`Hybrid RTL<hybrid_rtl>` section for :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` = 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:17
#: 390cc3b96e2a4f2ebff3b36b6dd5e112
msgid "If a pure VTOL QRTL is desired, then you must disable the fixed wing RTL and approach feature by setting :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16. Then the following actions will then occur on a QRTL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:19
#: 054d5b38fc414ab9aea4e06da7b0d8eb
msgid "The QuadPlane will immediately navigate towards the home location at :ref:`Q_WP_SPD<Q_WP_SPD>`, climbing or descending towards the :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` altitude. Once arriving within :ref:`Q_WP_RADIUS_M<Q_WP_RADIUS_M>` distance of home, it will begin descending at :ref:`Q_WP_SPD_DN<Q_WP_SPD_DN>` rate, until it reaches :ref:`Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT<Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT>` at which point it will descend at :ref:`Q_LAND_FINAL_SPD<Q_LAND_FINAL_SPD>` until landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:26
#: 1b3ebc890bb84c80b9bef47b557ac8c5
msgid "QuadPlane will recognize that it has landed if the motors are at minimum for 5 seconds and its altitude has not changed more than 0.2m for 4 seconds.  It does not use the altitude itself to decide whether to shut off the motors except that the QuadPlane must also be below :ref:`Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT<Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT>` above home(ie in the LAND FINAL phase). The altitude change for the decision can be increased, in case the altitude determination from the EKF is excessively noisy by increasing the :ref:`Q_LAND_ALTCHG<Q_LAND_ALTCHG>` value from its default value of 0.2m."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:32
#: 7877930aa1814f3396816559419cef0a
msgid "Alternatively, you may :ref:`configure the plane to return to a Rally Point <common-rally-points>`, rather than the home location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:36
#: 882fd5c374a94e70b39c220d07bf690d
msgid "\"Home\" position is always supposed to be your Plane's actual GPS takeoff location:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:39
#: 8ea7e08f2af144c6b80f5f88b1e6442f
msgid "It is very important to acquire GPS lock before arming in order for QRTL, QLOITER, AUTO or any GPS dependent mode to work properly. This requirement is provided in  the default arming checks. It is highly recommended that this check is not disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:41
#: c1f982478a8b42ac8b16c2d204e82a1b
msgid "For QuadPlane the home position is initially established at the time the plane acquires its GPS lock. It is then continuously updated as long as the autopilot is disarmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:45
#: 5da47ae4077f4061a76acfe387771320
msgid "This means if you execute an QRTL in QuadPlane, it will return to the location where it was when it was armed - assuming it had acquired GPS lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:46
#: 60c643dc2a9a4299b84647bd8dbe9092
msgid "Consider the use of :ref:`Rally Points <common-rally-points>` to avoid returning directly to your arming point on QRTL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:51
#: afb0b6f94e334c1e87fc36eb269ea6bb
msgid "In QRTL mode the autopilot uses a barometer which measures air pressure as the primary means for determining altitude (\"Pressure Altitude\") and if the air pressure is changing in your flight area, the copter will follow the air pressure change rather than actual altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:59
#: 06c483dcc3f74458a6a453a54c38d39b
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:62
#: 7ef0248891b8421b8d5097feac7ae6e2
msgid "Landing and re-arming the QuadPlane will reset home, which is a great feature for flying at airfields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qrtl-mode.rst:64
#: 8e15b9de0feb4c91b1082b2c2ecb1af4
msgid "If you get lock for the first time while flying, your home will be set at the location of lock."
msgstr ""
